    "28": {
      "date": "2026-10-28",
      "edition": "Wednesday 28 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coaching outlook",
          "heading": "Jake White says Fiji can be a massive force at World Cup",
          "body": "Jake White has backed Fiji to make a real impact at next year's World Cup in Australia, saying that if he can assemble the best 33 players for the tournament, they \"can be a massive force\". The former Springbok coach made the case after Fiji's 34-28 win over Japan in Tokyo, a game he played without any Europe-based players and in which he handed out four new caps. White's view is that Fiji can beat anyone on their day, provided the squad gets control and structure."
        },
