    "388": {
      "date": "2026-10-28",
      "edition": "Wednesday 28 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury blow",
          "heading": "Garry Ringrose ruled out of Ireland's November Tests with hamstring injury",
          "body": "Garry Ringrose is unlikely to be involved in Ireland's three home Nations Championship Tests, the IRFU said on Tuesday, and will continue his hamstring rehabilitation with Leinster. The 31-year-old, who has 76 caps, missed Leinster's URC win over Munster at the weekend. Andy Farrell has decided against calling up any replacements, despite uncertainty over Tadhg Furlong's availability. Sam Prendergast remains a doubt for the Argentina opener with a wrist injury."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "South Africa's Cheslin Kolbe set to miss rest of Nations Championship",
          "body": "Australia's Angus Crichton commits to NSW Waratahs after NRL switch. France's Galthié reshuffles Nations Championship squad after injuries. Wales release Rio Dyer from autumn squad with hamstring injury."
