      "edition": "Wednesday 28 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coaching belief",
          "heading": "Townsend insists Scotland now believe they can beat the All Blacks",
          "body": "Gregor Townsend says Scotland now believe they can beat New Zealand, a feeling his playing generation never had. Recalling the 62-31 and 69-20 defeats he suffered as a player, he told the BBC's Scotland Rugby Podcast: \"It's almost like two different lifetimes.\" As coach he has faced the All Blacks three times, all in Edinburgh, losing 25-17, 31-23 and 22-17. He concedes Scotland may have lacked composure in those games, but says the belief is there."
        },
        {
